DCPRO GhostGuard Kobo v0.8.3 Protect Beta

PROTECT CAN BECOME ACTIVE ONLY AFTER:
1. Profile V5 is READY and manually activated.
2. Two Shadow probation sessions pass.
3. A uinput virtual touchscreen is created successfully.
4. Nickel is verified to have opened the virtual input device.
5. Only then is EVIOCGRAB armed on the physical touchscreen.

QUARANTINE_MS=10
FAIL_OPEN=1

Any uinput write failure, input read failure, SYN_DROPPED, or process exit releases
EVIOCGRAB. If uinput is unavailable or Nickel does not open the virtual device,
Protect stays OFF and normal physical touch remains available.

The first 10 ms of a contact are buffered. Only high-confidence ultra-short ghost
candidates meeting the independent evidence-family gate are dropped. Longer or
multitouch contacts are forwarded conservatively.

License validation remains fail-closed for starting GhostGuard; touch handling is
fail-open so a Protect fault must not intentionally leave the physical screen grabbed.
